DrawDiagonal() draws the reference line marking where MAE equals MFE. That line is not drawn at a fixed forty-five degrees, because the two axes are usually scaled to different maximums. The method maps both endpoints through their own axis scale, so the line stays correct regardless of how the two maximums compare. Everything above it has more favorable than adverse excursion, exactly the region an efficiency above 0.5 corresponds to.
